  "id": "46cef00c-ddfc-5c51-8d07-113a2147f10d",
  "slug": "pasta-with-yogurt-sauce",
  "name": "Pasta with Yogurt Sauce",
  "recipe_type": "side",
  "brief_description": "Mash cloves of garlic into a paste and add to plain yogurt to make a tart and pungent pasta sauce. Toss with warm buttery noodles and garnish with parsley. Toasted pine nuts sprinkled over the top make this dish a special treat.",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Cook the pasta in a large pot of boiling salted water until al dente."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Using a mortar and pestle, mash the salt and garlic cloves together into a paste. Warm the yogurt slightly in a sauce pan. Remove a small amount of warmed yogurt from the pan, and stir together with the garlic paste. Stir this mixture into the remaining yogurt"
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Drain the pasta, and rinse in cold water. Place in a casserole or deep serving dish, toss with 1 tablespoon butter or margarine. Toss with half of the garlic-yogurt sauce. Spread the remaining sauce over the pasta. Garnish with the parsley."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "For a very special dish, brown the pine nuts in 2 tablespoons butter or margarine. Pour over the parsley. Serve immediately."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 7,
